    "result_text": "Build passes, tests green, and the audit output confirms the membership number is unchanged (`NSW-16E6609E-M26`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with the finding and centralized the two-digit fiscal-year rendering:\n\n- **`FiscalYear.java`** \u2014 added `public static String twoDigitStartYear(LocalDate)` as the single owner of the `% 100` + `%02d` formatting; `label(...)` now builds on it (`\"FY\" + twoDigitStartYear(date)`).\n- **`MembershipNumber.of`** \u2014 now calls `FiscalYear.twoDigitStartYear(...)` instead of re-implementing `String.format(\"%02d\", startYearOf(...) % 100)`. The two sides can no longer drift.\n\nI also took the reviewer's optional suggestion: since `label(LocalDate)` has no external callers, I made it **private**, keeping `FiscalYear`'s public surface to the owner-facing `of(Owner)` plus the two reusable primitives the sibling classes consume (`startYearOf`, `twoDigitStartYear`).\n\nBehaviour is unchanged \u2014 the membership number, fiscal year label, and tenure logic all produce identical values; this was a pure structural dedup.",
